---
title: The Locked Door
state:
  has_key: false
---

@scene start

You wake up in a small stone room. Sunlight cuts through a *narrow* window, and there is a **heavy** wooden door across from you. Something small glints on the windowsill — you can just make out the shape with a bit of `focus`.

## The Door

@background stone-room.svg

A [worn brass key](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Key_(lock)) sits within reach.

@layer brass-key.svg

@camera zoom to=1.3 duration=800ms

A closer look confirms it.

@camera zoom to=1

@sfx key-pickup.wav

@set has_key = true

@choice
- Take the key and try the door -> hallway-key
- Ignore it and try the door anyway -> hallway-plain
@end

@scene hallway-key

@background hallway.svg
@music hallway-theme.mp3

The key turns smoothly. The door swings open onto a long stone hallway.

Ahead, daylight spills in from an open archway.

@goto ending

@scene hallway-plain

@music hallway-theme.mp3

You throw your shoulder against the door. It doesn't budge — but a moment later, it creaks open anyway. Someone left it unlocked. The stone room is still at your back.

Ahead, daylight spills in from an open archway.

@goto ending

@scene ending

@pause 1s

You step out into the light. The story ends here, for now.
